%description:

Tcp.swsOverrideAfterRto:rfc-lower -- with an RTO below 0.1 s, the override timeout of the sender SWS avoidance is 0.1 s.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "false: the RTO held in the range 0.1 s to 1.0 s of the RFC, at most maxPersistTimeout". RFC
9293 section 3.8.6.2.1: "The override timeout should be in the range 0.1 - 1.0 seconds."

The classes: rfc-upper and rfc-lower (false): the RTO held in the range 0.1 s to 1.0 s; linux (true; the value of
LinuxTcp): one RTO. The code: TcpAlgorithmBase::startPersistTimer() and processPersistTimer(). This test separates
"rfc-lower" from "linux".

Host under test: host1, with an MSS of 1000 bytes and a minimum RTO of 10 ms, sends 5000 bytes. The round trip of the
network is below 1 ms, so the RTO of host1 is 10 ms. The TS option takes 12 bytes of each segment, so a full segment
holds 988 bytes. Peer: host2, with an advertised window of 3464 bytes, reads nothing. After three segments, 2964
bytes, the window of host2 is 500 bytes, and host1 holds the rest. Observation: level 1, host1 sends no data for 90 ms
after the hold, and sends the held data 0.1 s after the hold, not one RTO after it.

%# parameter: Tcp.swsOverrideAfterRto
%# class: rfc-lower
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.swsOverrideAfterRto
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSwsOverrideAfterRtoRfcLower")
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().setAutoRead(false);
            app.socket().bind(1000);
            app.socket().listen();
        }))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.window == 500")
             .describe("the ACK of host2 that leaves a window of 500 bytes: host1 holds its data")
             .within(1.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("held data before 0.1 s after the hold")
              .within(0.09))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the held data, 0.1 s after the hold")
             .within(0.02));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSwsOverrideAfterRtoRfcLower compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.swsOverrideAfterRto = false    # the parameter under test
**.tcp.mss = 1000
*.host1.tcp.minRexmitTimeout = 10ms
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 3464
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 5000B
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSwsOverrideAfterRtoRfcLower: PASS
